bside-trace 1
# Gate edges swept over every rate-counter offset: attack, decay and release all at the
# same rate r (r = 0, period 9, and r = 1, period 32), so the rate counter runs with one
# period throughout and successive trials start one cycle later in its cycle. Per trial
# the edge and the next 7 cycles are probed. T1: gate on from a frozen counter at 0, then
# gate off 40 cycles later (during attack). T2: gate off from sustain at 0xff (divider 1),
# then gate on during the release. T4: gate off while the decay runs (sustain 0). T3:
# sustain 5 (counter 0x55, divider 2), gate off at offsets over two periods, then gate on
# during the release 20 periods later (21 in the second half: the other divider parity).
# Oscillator 3, no waveform.
